    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0321" n="311" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/3887: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-14T10:00:00+01:00">June 14, 1943—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1096. For Lehman from Murphy, from Hoehler. Reference to the Department’s number
                    1130 [<hi rendition="#italic">1103</hi>]. Staff agrees that it might be
                    desirable to set up colony here for miscellaneous refugees now in Spain. <pb
                        facs="0322" n="312" xml:id="pg312"/> Discussed with Royce.<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d308-f1"/> Will discuss with French and Army and give you definite
                    reply later. Supplies in subsistence reserve and army stores available would in
                    our opinion meet food and clothing needs. Would attempt to add some subsistence
                    farm and self-help features to colony. Maintenance costs 1 year for 1000 people
                    over and above available supplies would approximate $100,000. Staff for
                    operation would approximate $25,000 more. Sending estimated construction costs
                    and more definite operating costs with a later wire. [Murphy and Hoehler.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d308-f1" n="80" xml:id="d308-f1-content">
                <p>Alexander B. Royce, Executive Chairman of the North African Economic Board and
                    Director of American Economic Operations in this theatre.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
